  ok       E1. two devices sending DIFFERENT random ids for the same (case, check-in type) both land on ONE deterministic key, so the upsert de-duplicates by construction rather than by a check
  ok       E2. CONTROL -- a payload MISSING case_id or checkin_type keeps its own id. A key built from a missing field would collide with every other row missing the same field, which is worse than the bug being fixed
